Use io.

Define local samples as array<whole number, 6>.
Set item 0 of samples to 7.
Set item 1 of samples to 9.
Set item 2 of samples to 11.
Set item 3 of samples to 13.
Set item 4 of samples to 15.
Set item 5 of samples to 17.
Let result be 0.
If every x in samples is more than 0, add 1 to result.
If some x in samples is more than 16, add 2 to result.
If no x in samples is less than 0, add 4 to result.
Say result.
Give back 0.
